<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  RUT_LongHunger - a Deep Desert leviathan contract. SANDWORM_MYTHOS_BUILD_1.

  Written against skills/rimworld-quests/SKILL.md, mirroring the proven shape of
  src/RimMandrake/StrandedQuest/Defs/QuestScriptDefs/Quest_Stranded.xml (GetMap ->
  GetNearbySettlement/asker -> reward value -> Delay isQuestTimeout -> GiveRewards
  + End). The one addition, QuestNode_CreateIncidents, is cited against real
  decompiled source (RimSage, RimWorld/QuestGen/QuestNode_CreateIncidents.cs) -
  not guessed.

  THE SPEC IT WAS BUILT FROM (skill SS2):
    ask         accept a salvage contract; the Long Hunger will surface on your
                own map during the delay window, deal with it (fight, flee,
                or just weather it out)
    reason      a nearby settlement's salvage crew went silent near a Dunes
                tile and wants to know why, without going themselves
    choice      implicit in play, not scripted: engage the creature for its
                loot (real risk, real reward) or stay clear and just collect
                the contract fee - both are legitimate, both survivable
    failure     nothing about the encounter itself can fail the quest (the
                creature always eventually submerges on its own timer,
                Thing.Tick handles that, see LongHungerThing.cs); the quest
                itself can only fail if the settlement goes hostile or the map
                is lost, same structural failure modes as Quest_Stranded
    reward      standard points-scaled contract fee (Util_GetDefaultRewardValueFromPoints),
                PLUS whatever salvage the creature drops on submerging - a
                bonus outside the formal contract, handled locally by
                LongHungerThing.Submerge(), not through the quest reward system
    deadline    the delay is the shown quest timer; the OFFER expires in 2-4
                days

  v1 DELIBERATE SIMPLIFICATIONS, named not hidden (see the item file for the
  full list):
  - Home-map encounter, not a distant travel/site quest like the reference mod
    (chezhou.creature.sandworm) - avoids the site-generation risk surface on a
    pass with no bridge to live-test against.
  - The Groundcaller (RUT_Groundcaller) is a normal buildable prop, not
    mechanically wired to the quest's own timer via a custom activation signal
    - the encounter fires on the quest's own accept-to-delay clock regardless
      of whether the player ever builds one. A real "build it, then it starts
      the clock" interactive loop is a named v2 improvement, not this pass's.
-->
<Defs>

  <QuestScriptDef>
    <defName>RUT_LongHungerContract</defName>

    <rootSelectionWeight>0.4</rootSelectionWeight>
    <rootMinPoints>0</rootMinPoints>
    <rootMinProgressScore>3</rootMinProgressScore>
    <minRefireDays>30</minRefireDays>
    <expireDaysRange>2~4</expireDaysRange>
    <defaultChallengeRating>3</defaultChallengeRating>
    <everAcceptableInSpace>true</everAcceptableInSpace>

    <questNameRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questName->RUT_LongHungerContract</li>
        <li>questName->The Long Hunger</li>
        <li>questName->Deep-Sand Contract</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questNameRules>

    <questDescriptionRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questDescription->[asker_nameDef] of [faction_name] sends word through a courier: a salvage crew went out toward the empty ground three days ago and has not answered since. The old stories call that ground the Long Hunger's - nothing survives on it long enough to leave wreckage behind, which is precisely why nobody else will go.\n\n[asker_nameDef] asks you to draw it out instead of walking onto its ground: build a groundcaller, let it run, and be ready for what answers. The Long Hunger surfaces within [surfaceTicks_duration] of accepting, does what it does, and goes back under inside the hour. Whatever it has been hoarding is yours if you can reach it before the sand closes again.\n\n[asker_nameDef]'s fee is for the answer, not the salvage.[caravanNote]</li>

        <li>caravanNote(canCaravan==False,priority=1)-> Your colony cannot reach [settlement_label] overland; word will have to reach you some other way.</li>
        <li>caravanNote-></li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questDescriptionRules>

    <root Class="QuestNode_Sequence">
      <nodes>

        <li Class="QuestNode_GetMap" />

        <li Class="QuestNode_GetNearbySettlement">
          <storeAs>settlement</storeAs>
          <storeFactionLeaderAs>asker</storeFactionLeaderAs>
          <storeCanCaravanAs>canCaravan</storeCanCaravanAs>
          <maxTileDistance>32</maxTileDistance>
        </li>
        <li Class="QuestNode_GetFactionOf">
          <thing>$asker</thing>
          <storeAs>faction</storeAs>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_SubScript">
          <def>Util_GetDefaultRewardValueFromPoints</def>
        </li>

        <!-- The shown timer AND the encounter clock. 8-14 in-game hours. -->
        <li Class="QuestNode_Set">
          <name>surfaceTicks</name>
          <value>$(randInt(8,14)*2500)</value>
        </li>

        <!-- points for QuestNode_CreateIncidents.TestRunInt - RUT_LongHungerSurfaces
             spans 0..99999 so this can never fail that gate (see the IncidentDef's
             own header comment). -->
        <li Class="QuestNode_Set">
          <name>encounterPoints</name>
          <value>1400</value>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_CreateIncidents">
          <incidentDef>RUT_LongHungerSurfaces</incidentDef>
          <randomIncidents>1</randomIncidents>
          <startOffsetTicks>$surfaceTicks</startOffsetTicks>
          <duration>$surfaceTicks</duration>
          <points>$encounterPoints</points>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_Delay">
          <delayTicks>$surfaceTicks</delayTicks>
          <isQuestTimeout>true</isQuestTimeout>
          <inspectString TKey="InspectStringTimeLeft">Time left: {0}</inspectString>
          <outSignalComplete>ContractDue</outSignalComplete>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_Letter">
          <inSignal>ContractDue</inSignal>
          <label TKey="LetterLabelLongHungerPaid">Contract closed</label>
          <letterDef>PositiveEvent</letterDef>
          <text TKey="LetterTextLongHungerPaid">The Long Hunger has gone back under. [asker_nameDef] considers the question answered and the contract fulfilled - whatever you took from the sand on the way is yours to keep, not theirs to ask about.</text>
        </li>
        <li Class="QuestNode_GiveRewards">
          <inSignal>ContractDue</inSignal>
          <parms>
            <allowGoodwill>true</allowGoodwill>
            <allowRoyalFavor>false</allowRoyalFavor>
          </parms>
        </li>
        <li Class="QuestNode_End">
          <inSignal>ContractDue</inSignal>
          <outcome>Success</outcome>
          <sendStandardLetter>false</sendStandardLetter>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_End">
          <inSignal>faction.BecameHostileToPlayer</inSignal>
          <outcome>Fail</outcome>
        </li>
        <li Class="QuestNode_End">
          <inSignal>map.MapRemoved</inSignal>
          <outcome>Fail</outcome>
        </li>

      </nodes>
    </root>
  </QuestScriptDef>

</Defs>
